[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_o0644")
dialogue_id = "debate_plague"
record_title = "Debate Speech: Plague"
text = "PAGE: historian(PORTAL_NETWORK), AUDIENCE
historian: I recently received a new museum exhibit from one of the shards.
historian: It is a human bone pierced by a thousand little holes.
historian: The scholars of that shard speak of a terrible bone-eating plague that once swept across the ancient world.
historian: We often look at our scattered shards and see only isolation, treating our separation as a tragedy that must be fixed.
historian: But we fail to see the advantages of our current state.
historian: A united world is a fragile world.
historian: When everyone shares the same roads, they also share the same disasters.
historian: If a sickness takes root in a unified empire, it will travel every highway until there is nowhere left to hide.
historian: The Cloud Sea ensures that if one shard falls, the rest of humanity survives.
historian: The Scribe wants to stitch the world back together.
historian: But if we remove all the empty space between us, we remove the gaps that keep a fire from spreading."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
